Authorization decisions in JSON, in protobuf and in the SAPL binary format, as the node sends them.

JSON leaves out empty obligations, empty advice and an undefined resource, and writes the fields
in the order decision, obligations, advice, resource. A whole number within 64 bits is written
plainly, whatever notation it came in. Any other number without exponent is written plainly, one
with an exponent in scientific notation unless it is a small negative one. Undefined and error
values have no JSON form. Protobuf is AuthorizationDecision of sapl_types.proto; fields that hold
their default are left out, and numbers are written plainly. The binary form (BINARY_FORMAT.md of
this crate) is the lead byte 00, the text region, the verdict byte, the obligations and the advice each as a count
and values, and the resource, undefined when absent.

The document holds the parts of the decision, one per line: 'decision' with its name, and
optionally 'obligations' and 'advice' as JSON arrays and 'resource' as JSON or as the word 'error'.
A missing part is empty or undefined. The expectation holds 'json' with the JSON form, or
'refused', 'protobuf' with the bytes in hexadecimal, which may go on in further lines, and
'binary' with the bytes of the binary form alike. A '//' starts a comment to the end of the line.

=== a permit
decision: PERMIT
---
json: {"decision":"PERMIT"}
protobuf: 08 01
binary: 00 00 01 00 00 00

=== a deny
decision: DENY
---
json: {"decision":"DENY"}
protobuf: 08 02
binary: 00 00 02 00 00 00

=== not applicable
decision: NOT_APPLICABLE
---
json: {"decision":"NOT_APPLICABLE"}
protobuf: 08 03
binary: 00 00 03 00 00 00

=== a suspend
decision: SUSPEND
---
json: {"decision":"SUSPEND"}
protobuf: 08 04
binary: 00 00 04 00 00 00

=== indeterminate, which in protobuf is the empty message
decision: INDETERMINATE
---
json: {"decision":"INDETERMINATE"}
protobuf:
binary: 00 00 00 00 00 00

=== empty obligations and advice
decision: PERMIT
obligations: []
advice: []
---
json: {"decision":"PERMIT"}
protobuf: 08 01
binary: 00 00 01 00 00 00

=== obligations, advice and a resource
decision: PERMIT
obligations: [{"type":"log"}]
advice: ["hint"]
resource: {"name":"Wilbur"}
---
json: {"decision":"PERMIT","obligations":[{"type":"log"}],"advice":["hint"],"resource":{"name":"Wilbur"}}
protobuf: 08 01
   12 13 0a 11 32 0f 0a 0d 0a 04 74 79 70 65 12 05 22 03 6c 6f 67    // obligations
   1a 08 0a 06 22 04 68 69 6e 74                                     // advice
   22 14 32 12 0a 10 0a 04 6e 61 6d 65 12 08 22 06 57 69 6c 62 75 72 // resource
binary: 00 15 74 79 70 65 6c 6f 67 68 69 6e 74 6e 61 6d 65 57 69 6c 62 75 72 01 01 61 04 23 01 24 61 04 26

=== a resource that is null
decision: PERMIT
resource: null
---
json: {"decision":"PERMIT","resource":null}
protobuf: 08 01 22 02 0a 00
binary: 00 00 01 00 00 01

=== a resource that is false
decision: PERMIT
resource: false
---
json: {"decision":"PERMIT","resource":false}
protobuf: 08 01 22 02 10 00
binary: 00 00 01 00 00 02

=== numbers in plain and in scientific notation
decision: PERMIT
obligations: [1E+3,1E-7,2.50,-0.5,123.456]
---
json: {"decision":"PERMIT","obligations":[1000,1E-7,2.50,-0.5,123.456]}
protobuf: 08 01 12 30
   0a 06 1a 04 31 30 30 30                     // "1000"
   0a 0b 1a 09 30 2e 30 30 30 30 30 30 31      // "0.0000001"
   0a 06 1a 04 32 2e 35 30                     // "2.50"
   0a 06 1a 04 2d 30 2e 35                     // "-0.5"
   0a 09 1a 07 31 32 33 2e 34 35 36            // "123.456"
binary: 00 00 01 05 04 d0 0f 05 02 0e 05 f4 03 04 05 09 02 05 80 89 0f 06 00 00

=== numbers at the border of the plain notation
decision: PERMIT
obligations: [0.000001,0.0000012,1000000,1e2,0.00]
---
json: {"decision":"PERMIT","obligations":[0.000001,0.0000012,1000000,100,0]}
binary: 00 00 01 05 05 02 0c 05 18 0e 04 80 89 7a e4 80 00 00

=== nested arrays and empty containers
decision: PERMIT
obligations: [[[],{}]]
---
json: {"decision":"PERMIT","obligations":[[[],{}]]}
protobuf: 08 01 12 0c 0a 0a 2a 08 0a 02 2a 00 0a 02 32 00
binary: 00 00 01 01 42 40 60 00 00

=== quotes, backslashes and control characters in a text
decision: PERMIT
obligations: ["a\"b\\c\n\u0001"]
---
json: {"decision":"PERMIT","obligations":["a\"b\\c\n\u0001"]}
protobuf: 08 01 12 0b 0a 09 22 07 61 22 62 5c 63 0a 01
binary: 00 07 61 22 62 5c 63 0a 01 01 01 27 00 00

=== characters outside ASCII and a slash
decision: PERMIT
advice: ["<U+00E9>/<U+1F600>"]
---
json: {"decision":"PERMIT","advice":["<U+00E9>/<U+1F600>"]}
binary: 00 07 c3 a9 2f f0 9f 98 80 01 00 01 27 00

=== an error as resource
decision: DENY
resource: error
---
json: refused
protobuf: 08 02 22 09 42 07 0a 05 42 6f 6f 6d 2e    // error "Boom."
binary: 00 05 42 6f 6f 6d 2e 02 00 00 07 05
